# 1️⃣1️⃣ 0/1 KNAPSACK ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

Each item can be:

```text
Take
OR
Don't Take
```

Given:

```text
Weight
Value
Capacity
```

We want maximum value without exceeding capacity.

---

## DP State

A common definition:

```text
dp[i][w]
```

means:

> Maximum value using the first `i` items with capacity `w`.

Choices:

### Don't take

```text
dp[i-1][w]
```

### Take

```text
value[i] + dp[i-1][w-weight[i]]
```

Therefore:

$$
dp[i][w]
=
\max(
dp[i-1][w],
value_i+dp[i-1][w-weight_i]
)
$$

